<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pohnpei</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ponape</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pohnpei is a volcanic island in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caroline-islands">Caroline Islands</a> of the western Pacific, the largest island of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federated-states-of-micronesia">Federated States of Micronesia</a> and home to its capital, Palikir. Under the Saudeleur dynasty, from roughly the 12th to the 17th century, it was ruled from Nan Madol, a complex of artificial islets built of basalt off its eastern shore. It was later divided into chiefdoms under Nahnmwarki and came under Spanish, German, Japanese and American rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pohnpei.jpg" alt="Pohnpei" width="320" height="314" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aotearoa · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pohnpei_Island.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
